<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- The audio-routing code reads the Bluetooth headset profile state to choose
         between speaker, receiver and Bluetooth — see
         PluginHandler.setSpeakerPhoneOnInternal and
         AudioNotificationListener.listenForRouteChanges. BLUETOOTH_CONNECT is
         required for that from API 31; BLUETOOTH covers older releases.

         Declaring them here means a consuming app does not have to. Both call sites
         report "no headset connected" when the grant is missing, so an app only needs
         to *request* BLUETOOTH_CONNECT if it wants Bluetooth routing to work; speaker
         and receiver routing function without it.

         Deliberately declared with no attributes. Setting android:maxSdkVersion here
         (30 would be the natural value for the legacy permission) makes the manifest
         merger fail the build of any app that declares the same permission with a
         different value — "Attribute uses-permission#...@maxSdkVersion value=(30) ...
         is also present at AndroidManifest.xml value=(29)". With the attribute absent
         the app's own declaration simply wins, whatever it says. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.BLUETOOTH" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.BLUETOOTH_CONNECT" />
</manifest>
